  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## v3.2.2 (patch)\n\nChanges since v3.2.1:\n\n- Regenerate stale package-validation suppressions [patch] (#180) (matt-edmondson)\n- Hide the selected-tab overline in unfocused windows [patch] (#165) (matt-edmondson)\n- Give Everforest and Nightfox an Alternate that isn't their Warning color [patch] (#169) (matt-edmondson)\n- Refuse a theme missing a meaning the ImGui mapper draws from [patch] (#168) (matt-edmondson)\n- Make ImGui's BorderShadow transparent, as the stock styles do [patch] (#170) (matt-edmondson)\n- Give Tokyo Night Storm and Day a purple Debug of their own [patch] (#173) (matt-edmondson)\n- Draw inner table lines lighter than the outer border [patch] (#174) (matt-edmondson)\n- Give the selected tab its own fill on the tab bar [patch] (#163) (matt-edmondson)\n- Keep input frames visible in striped table rows [patch] (#162) (matt-edmondson)\n- Give Kanagawa Dragon its own pink and violet for Alternate and Debug [patch] (#159) (matt-edmondson)\n- Use Assert.Contains for the Neutral message checks (MSTEST0046) (Claude)\n- Refuse a theme with no Neutral colors in MakeCompletePalette (Claude)\n- Refuse a SemanticPalette with no neutrals, and name unassigned accents [patch] (Claude)\n- Match theme families case-insensitively [patch] (Claude)\n- Bring the README sample and lightness-band docs up to date (matt-edmondson)\n- Seed the chroma search with the achromatic color at the target lightness (matt-edmondson)",
